   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Turkmenistan President Saparmurad Niyazov smiles in this May 19, 2000 photo. An unidentified attacker, who was in a truck, fired on Niyazov's car with a submachine gun on Monday morning Nov. 25 in Ashgabat, a government official said. Niyazov was not injured in what the leader called an assassination attempt. Known as Turkmenbashi _ or ``Father of All Turkmen'' _ Niyazov rules his impoverished but energy-rich Central Asian nation with an iron hand.(AP Photo/Alexander Zemlianichenko)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:creator>
